course: dictionary
lesson: 609
title: Awkward: embarrassed, clumsy or hard to handle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Awkward has several meanings, and the words around it show which one is meant. «A phone call with a parent you rarely see can feel awkward, and that is okay.» Here awkward means uncomfortable, the feeling you get when you don't know what to say.
explain: «Real bears ... it is slow and awkward» means clumsy, moving in a way that is not smooth. «Its short, thick, muscly neck just makes it awkward» means hard to deal with, because of the pig's shape.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «an awkward silence» still make sense if you think "an uncomfortable silence"? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Awkward means uncomfortable or embarrassing, when you don't know what to say or do.
fact: Awkward also means clumsy, moving in a way that is not smooth.
fact: Awkward can mean hard to use, carry or deal with, because of its shape or situation.
fact: An awkward person is hard to get along with.
fact: Useful phrases: «an awkward silence», «feel awkward», «an awkward shape», «awkward to carry».
exercise: «A phone call with a parent you rarely see can feel awkward.» What does awkward mean here? | *Uncomfortable, not knowing what to say | Clumsy, moving badly | Happy and excited | Very loud
exercise: «Real bears walk a few steps upright, but it is slow and awkward.» What does awkward mean here? | Quiet and calm | Hard to get along with | Embarrassing for the bear | *Clumsy, not smooth
exercise: Which phrase means a long, uncomfortable quiet? | a loud cheer | a tall tree | *an awkward silence | a cold drink
test: «Its short, thick, muscly neck just makes it awkward.» What does awkward mean here? | Full of light | Quick and smooth | Very happy | *Hard to deal with because of its shape
test: «Alice leads a crowd of soggy birds to the shore: a funny, slightly awkward scene.» What does awkward mean here? | Lucky | Shiny | *Embarrassing | Dangerous
exam: Which word means hard to get along with, as in «an awkward person»? | Barely | *Awkward | Glum | Gentle
